<p>In a regulatory development with global implications, Dubai's Virtual Assets Regulatory Authority (VARA) updated its anti-money laundering guidelines on 17 June, requiring all crypto firms operating in the emirate to integrate real-time screening against the Financial Action Task Force (FATF) blacklist. Firms now have 90 days to implement the changes.</p>

